Cell["XMLCases::badpat: The second argument should be a pattern, or a rule pattern -> rhs or pattern :> rhs. A pattern is an XMLPattern, which can take constraints on the elements below it, an XMLDocument pattern, an XMLElement pattern, or a CSS selector string, or alternatives of these, any of them named, with a condition pat /; test or a test pat?f. A CSS selector that depends on what is above or beside the element it selects, such as \"nav a\", gives that element when given alone; on the left of a rule, name the element, as in n : \"nav a\" :> n. Got \"nav a\".", "Message", "MSG"],

